%N A398529 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} omega(k)/(k*(k+1)), where omega(k) = A001221(k) is the number of distinct primes dividing k.
%C A398529 This constant appears in the asymptotic formula for A398528.
%H A398529 Olivier Bordellès, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1142/S1793042122501056">On certain sums of number theory</a>, International Journal of Number Theory, Vol. 18, No. 9  (2022), pp. 2053-2074; <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.05751v2">arXiv preprint</a>, arXiv:2009.05751 [math.NT], 2020.
%H A398529 Mihoub Bouderbala and Meselem Karras, <a href="http://doi.org/10.7546/nntdm.2020.26.4.52-56">On a sum involving the number of distinct prime factors function related to the integer part function</a>, Notes on Number Theory and Discrete Mathematics, Vol. 26, No. 4 (2020), pp. 52-56.
%H A398529 Kui Liu, Jie Wu, and Zhishan Yang, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1142/S179304212450043X">On some sums involving the integral part function</a>, International Journal of Number Theory, Vol. 20, No. 3 (2024), pp. 831-847; <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.01382">arXiv preprint</a>, arXiv:2109.01382 [math.NT], 2021.
%F A398529 Equals Sum_{k>=2} (-1)^k * D(k), where D(s) = zeta(s) * prime_zeta(s) is the Dirichlet g.f. of omega.
%e A398529 0.591845878310049824648351814607086786452855786471936...
%o A398529 (PARI) suminf(k = 2, (-1)^k * zeta(k) * sumeulerrat(1/p, k))
%Y A398529 Cf. A001221, A398528.
